{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-18T03:20:14.848Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"596c556c2cee537407898227","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-18T03:20:14.848Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Persistence regression found that normalized SDK settings callbacks omit opaque package sections: a later task receipt could replace earlier calibrations. Fixed by reading the opaque Jev section through the SDK while holding the audited mutation lock, then merging the task/model key. Regression verifies both prior calibrations and unrelated Jev settings survive. Calibrated link inference now uses the same pairwise state as evaluation; legacy batching remains unchanged. Source checks, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks have passed; full coverage measurement is running."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-18T03:20:14.848Z"}],"before_hash":"040c94bbeac0b2d76618e96c560f326642650857dd9bbb9f3dc7f81a3bfb8601","after_hash":"3f1f1ad439f288a6dab15cbc64e5881bf2523d619a39df716e1165450f1a2072","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"cbc1b16200132cb8d50f8b86a6a055a9f790f33bdc2ec492bb288a03f49c99f3"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-18T03:33:54.353Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"596c556c2cee537407898227","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-18T03:33:54.353Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Independent behavioural revert proofs: (1) restoring only decideTriage from origin/main makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"calibrated triage uses\" test/calibrated-decisions.test.ts fail 0/1 at the calibrated-probability assertion. (2) removing only the calibration-repository filter in calibrateObservations makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"temperature minimizes\" test/decision-calibration.test.ts fail 0/1: held-out label changes move temperature from 0.05 to 20. (3) replacing only the locked opaque settings read in runEvaluationCommand with normalized current.jev makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"calibrate persists\" test/evaluation-command.test.ts fail 0/1 because the existing keep_alive setting disappears. All mutants exited 1 with assertion failures, no timeouts; all three source files restored byte-for-byte. Tests import TypeScript directly, so no rebuild is needed for these proofs. Corrected focused suite previously passed 14/14; final added identity/retrieval cases are rerunning."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-18T03:33:54.353Z"}],"before_hash":"3f1f1ad439f288a6dab15cbc64e5881bf2523d619a39df716e1165450f1a2072","after_hash":"ad5022510e6389676d0c73941f1cbcd64cf317ea0ba41ec87fbcf68af88f44fe","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_