{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-18T03:50:54.521Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"596c556c2cee537407898227","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-18T03:50:54.521Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Corrected focused suite passes 16/16. All three new modules measured 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines in the dedicated coverage run. Final policy regressions cover unqualified streaming, changed schemas, missing channels, removal of calibration, model replacement during inference and stricter explicit confidence flags. Calibration defaults to 100 requests (evaluation 40), because a 40-case split cannot reach the 0.9 one-sided precision bound even if perfect. No live target or standard was lowered. SDK operation IDs are invocation-scoped so reapplying an intentionally removed calibration is not mistaken for replay. Compatibility inspection confirms the declared host floor exports both repeatable flags and audited settings mutation; dependency pins and release policy remain unchanged. The first full npm gate passed 184 tests but failed coverage during edits; the first Bun gate exposed a synthetic operation-ID replay bug and missing streaming branches. Those are corrected; neither failed gate is counted as a pass. Final isolated full gates follow."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-18T03:50:54.521Z"}],"before_hash":"152806ce73a5275be95e3bf91c77b05b5d0f97bdf8736346c6db498adb0d183a","after_hash":"aaf4a800bd555d157b515abb5aab7b1d86400b3c17287d84a0932d8f2c9671b9","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effo